>> title: Hong Kong Borscht
>> category: Soups
>> tags: tomato, cabbage, beef, hong kong, soup, one pot
>> counters: Cha Chaan Teng
>> aka: lo song tong, lo sung tong, 羅宋湯, 紅湯, Borsch Soup, Hong Kong borscht, Russian soup, red soup, 餐湯
>> pairs-with: borscht
>> servings: 6
>> time: 1 hr 30 min
>> slack: forgiving — an hour longer only softens the cabbage further and it is better reheated the next day, so nothing in it is a window you can miss

There is no beetroot in this. It is not the Ukrainian soup — the name travelled through Shanghai.

>> step: brown 8 min in the fat that comes out
Brown @beef shin{12%oz}(340 g; in 1-in cubes) in @neutral oil{1%Tbs} in a #Dutch oven{} for ~brown{8%min}.

>> step: sweat 8 min
Sweat @yellow onion{1%large}(diced), @celery{2%ribs}(sliced) and @carrot{1%large}(in half-moons) into @&(~1)beef{} for ~sweat{8%min}.

>> step: simmer 1 hr, lid ajar
Simmer @&(~1)pot{} with @tomato paste{2%Tbs}, @canned chopped tomatoes{14%oz}(400 g), @russet potato{1%large}(cubed), @green cabbage{4%cups}(shredded), @beef stock{6%cups}(1.4 L) and @bay leaf{1} for ~simmer{1%hr} with the lid ajar.

>> step: season, and taste it for sweet against sour
Season @&(~1)soup{} with @kosher salt{2%tsp}, @sugar{2%tsp}, @Worcestershire sauce{1%Tbs} and @black pepper{1/2%tsp}.
